    <span class="eyebrow">About Us</span>
    <h1>Practical Farming Knowledge, Rooted in Real Research</h1>
    <p class="lede">GoOrganicAfrica is built around one simple idea: farming knowledge should be practical, tested, and shared freely across Africa.</p>

    <h2>Who We Are</h2>
    <p>GoOrganicAfrica's guides and tools are built by {{ site.author }} — a farmer, agricultural researcher, and organic bio-fertilizer producer holding a certificate in Agriculture since 2001. Every guide and every data point in our free <a href="/farm-profit-calculator/">Farm Profit Calculator</a> comes from real production experience and continuous agricultural research, not theory alone.</p>

    <h2>What We Do</h2>
    <p>Beyond research and writing, the work behind GoOrganicAfrica spans several organic agricultural products:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>InoculumPlus</strong> — a Mycorrhiza-based organic bio-fertilizer sold to farmers across Nigeria, Cameroon and Niger Republic</li>
      <li><strong>OrganicGrow</strong> — an organic solution for poultry, fish and other livestock that has reached farmers in Cameroon and Ivory Coast</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Our Tools and Guides</h2>
    <p>We provide two core resources for African farmers:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong><a href="/farm-profit-calculator/">Free Farm Profit Calculator</a></strong> — calculate your cost of production, expected revenue, profit, ROI and break-even point across {{ site.calculator.countryCount }} African countries and {{ site.calculator.enterpriseCount }} farming enterprises, with automatic currency switching</li>
      <li><strong><a href="/ebooks/">Organic Farming Guides</a></strong> — step-by-step practical guides on hydroponic fodder farming, black soldier fly farming, oyster mushroom farming and weed-free cassava production</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Our Mission</h2>
    <p>To help make farming across Nigeria, Africa and the wider world more profitable and more sustainable — one practical, farm-tested guide and tool at a time. Read our latest insights on the <a href="/blog/">GoOrganicAfrica farming blog</a>.</p>

    <h2>External Resources We Trust</h2>
    <p>For farmers seeking additional agricultural data and research, we recommend:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://www.fao.org/home/en" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">FAO (Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations)</a> — global agricultural statistics and research</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.iita.org" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">IITA (International Institute of Tropical Agriculture)</a> — Africa-focused crop and farming research</li>
    </ul>

